    <div style="background: #f0f7f7; border-left: 4px solid var(--brand); border-radius: 0 14px 14px 0; padding: 24px; margin-bottom: 32px;">
      <h2 style="font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 36px); margin-bottom: 14px; color: var(--brand-dark);">What Is Vacation Rental Property Management?</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.85;">Vacation rental property management means handling the operational, revenue, guest-service, and compliance work that keeps a short-term rental profitable without burning out the owner. For Gulf Coast owners, that usually includes dynamic pricing, listing optimization, professional cleaning and maintenance coordination, guest screening, local support, and reporting that shows what the property is actually earning. At Seascape Vacations, we focus on the Bradenton-Sarasota corridor, where owners often need a manager who understands both beach-driven traveler demand and the neighborhood-level rules that affect Anna Maria Island, Bradenton, Sarasota, Siesta Key, and Longboat Key. If you want the location-specific detail, start with our <a href="/property-management/vacation-rental-management-bradenton/">Bradenton</a>, <a href="/property-management/vacation-rental-management-sarasota/">Sarasota</a>, and <a href="/property-management/vacation-rental-management-anna-maria-island/">Anna Maria Island</a> service pages.</p>
    </div>

    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(260px,1fr));gap:24px;margin-bottom:32px;">
      <div style="background:white;border-radius:18px;padding:24px;box-shadow:0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);">
        <p class="section-tag" style="margin-bottom:10px;">Revenue</p>
        <h2 style="font-size:24px;margin-bottom:12px;color:var(--brand-dark);">Pricing + Occupancy Strategy</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--stone-light);margin-bottom:0;">We manage nightly rates, minimum stays, and seasonality so owners stop leaving money on the table during peak Gulf Coast demand.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:white;border-radius:18px;padding:24px;box-shadow:0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);">
        <p class="section-tag" style="margin-bottom:10px;">Operations</p>
        <h2 style="font-size:24px;margin-bottom:12px;color:var(--brand-dark);">Local Guest + Vendor Support</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--stone-light);margin-bottom:0;">Owners need real local coverage for turnovers, guest issues, inspections, and maintenance coordination. That is where remote managers usually break down.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:white;border-radius:18px;padding:24px;box-shadow:0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);">
        <p class="section-tag" style="margin-bottom:10px;">Reporting</p>
        <h2 style="font-size:24px;margin-bottom:12px;color:var(--brand-dark);">Clear Owner Visibility</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--stone-light);margin-bottom:0;">Performance only matters if owners can understand it. We treat reporting as an operating tool, not a monthly afterthought.</p>
